This notice describes the current behavior of the Yanami desktop application. The
publisher should publish this document at a public URL and review it before
submitting the app to any store. This notice is not legal advice.

## Data and processing

- **First-run consent:** The app blocks its main features until the user accepts
  the in-app privacy notice and [Terms of Use](./TERMS.md). Declining closes the
  app and does not save acceptance. The acceptance version and timestamp are
  stored in Godot's local per-user application data. A user can withdraw
  consent in Settings; this removes the saved acceptance and closes the app.
  The notices appear again at the next launch.
- **Wake-word microphone:** When enabled, the microphone waits for “Yanami”.
  Vosk performs wake-word recognition locally on the device; wake-word audio is
  not sent to a cloud service. The wake-word toggle can be turned off.
- **Manual microphone:** When the user turns on manual listening, the app
  records a spoken phrase and sends its audio to Google's speech-recognition
  service for transcription. Manual listening can be turned off with its
  toggle. Microphone availability and processing also depend on Windows and
  installed audio components.
- **Chat and AI providers:** Chat text, the system instructions/profile, and
  recent conversation messages are sent to the selected AI provider. Ollama
  can run locally on the user's computer. If an external API is selected, that
  provider receives the request and handles it under its own terms and privacy
  policy. API availability, retention, and charges are determined by that
  provider.
- **Local conversation data:** Up to 100 recent chat entries are persisted in
  `%APPDATA%/MiAvatar/verity_chat_history.json`. The app also stores its
  configuration and profile under `%APPDATA%/MiAvatar/`. The API key is
  protected using Windows DPAPI and is not stored in the configuration JSON.
- **Spoken responses:** Neural speech uses Microsoft Edge TTS over the Internet
  and sends the reply text to that service. If it fails, the app attempts to
  use Windows SAPI locally.
- **Screen and camera:** Visual permissions start disabled. A screen or camera
  image is captured only after the user enables `PERMISOS` and explicitly
  presses `VER PANTALLA` or `VER CÁMARA`. The requested image is sent to the
  active AI model for analysis. The app does not continuously stream screen
  or camera images.
- **PC actions:** PC control starts disabled and requires both visual
  permissions and the separate PC-control toggle. It runs only the explicit
  actions supported by the app, not arbitrary model-generated shell commands.
- **Active window observation:** When enabled, the app periodically reads and
  displays the active window title. It does not capture the window image.
- **Mood indicator:** The neutral/happy/sad/angry estimate is derived locally
  from message wording. It is approximate and is not a diagnosis.

## Third-party services and requirements

Depending on the features and configuration used, Yanami may communicate with
Google speech recognition, Microsoft Edge TTS, Ollama, or a user-selected
OpenAI-compatible API such as Google Gemini, OpenAI, OpenRouter, Groq, DeepSeek,
or another custom endpoint. Review the chosen provider's privacy policy and
terms before use. Voice and AI features may require Python packages, Internet
access, and/or separately installed Ollama software and models.

## User choices and deletion

Users can disable wake-word listening, turn manual listening off, disable
visual permissions, disable PC control, and stop using the application.
Conversation history and configuration files can be removed by the user from
`%APPDATA%/MiAvatar/`. Withdrawing consent removes the saved consent decision;
it does not erase data already sent to third-party providers. Data held by a
third-party provider is subject to that provider's own policies and controls.

